==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ang|þenċean}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*þankijaną}}. Cognate with {{cog|ofs|thenka}} ({{cog|fy|tinke}}), {{cog|osx|thenkian}} ({{cog|nds|denken}}), {{cog|odt|thenken}} ({{cog|nl|denken}}), {{cog|goh|thenken}} ({{cog|de|denken}}), {{cog|non|þekkja}} ({{cog|gmq-osw|þækkia}}, {{cog|is|þekkja}}), {{cog|got|𐌸𐌰𐌲𐌺𐌾𐌰𐌽}}. All ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*teng-||to think}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈθent͡ʃan/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|head=þenċan}}

# to [[think]]

